  "ExportFileNameIdentifierTooltipText": "Optional text for the file name\n(position is defined in the filename format)",
  "ExportFileNameStructureTooltipText": "Define how the file name is built (e.g., label + date + process)",
  "ExportSubfolderTooltipText": "Files are automatically exported into\nsubfolders created based on the selected time unit.\n\nExamples:\nDaily: 20260101\nWeekly: 2026-W01 (ISO week number)\nMonthly: 2026-01",
  "ExportFileSplitTooltipText": "Prevents creating oversized files.\nIf the row limit or 100MB size is exceeded,\nthe output is split into multiple files.\n\nSplit files are numbered (e.g., dat_1.csv, dat_2.csv).",
  "masterTypeSuffixMeasurement": "measurement",
  "masterTypeSuffixHistory": "history",
  "Multi-axis Plot": "Multi-axis Plot",
  "Multi-axis Plot Hint": "Splits graphs by variables or category values.\nIt is suitable for visualizing small to medium-scale datasets and useful for comparing categories or tracking multiple variables at the same time.",
  "Layout hover messenger": "After selecting the primary variable(s), specify the additional data to display.\n\nCommon settings (applied to all primary variables)\n   X-axis (optional): Select the variable to use for the X-axis. If omitted, data order is used.\n   Lab: Specify the label displayed in the plot.\n   LabX: Display labels using the X-axis values.\n   Color: Color-code data by the variable's category values.\n   ColorX: Color-code data by the X-axis category values.\n   ColImb: Display categories with extremely small values on a secondary axis.\n   ColImbX: Color-code the categories displayed on the secondary axis.\n       - Only the top 16 categories by data count are displayed. Categories with the same count are ordered by date/time.\n       - When Color (Imb) is selected, settings cannot be configured individually for each primary variable.\n\nSettings for each primary variable\n Specify the data to add or split for each primary variable.\n(The numeric prefix indicates the order in which the primary variables were selected.)\n   1-Lab: Specify the label to display for this primary variable.\n   1-Step: Specify a step variable (used to display thresholds or control values).\n\nOverlay multiple variables\n   1-Main: Add a variable to the primary (left) axis.\n   1-2nd: Add a variable to the secondary (right) axis (up to 3 variables).\n   1-Auto: Overlay a variable without assigning it to an axis.\n       - Up to 8 variables can be specified per primary variable (1-Main + 1-2nd + 1-Auto + 1-Step).\n\nSplit by category values\n   1Color: Color-code data by the variable's category values.\n   1ColImb: Display categories with extremely small values on a secondary axis.\n       - Up to 8 category values are displayed (only the top 8 categories by data count).\n",
  "MAP plot style hover msg": "Select the data rendering method.\n— Auto: Line Plot + Markers for main variables only (default for a small number of data points)\n— Line: Line plot\n-•- Line+Marker: Line plot with markers\n• Marker: Marker-only scatter plot (default for a large number of data points)\n",
  "MAP y-axis hover msg": "Switch the display mode for plots using Color or the primary axis only.\nNormal: Standard line chart (raw values). Auto Log Scale\nStack: Stacked line chart (raw values).\n%: Percentage line chart.\n%Stack: Stacked percentage line chart (composition ratio).\nLog Off: Display using a linear scale only.\nLog On: Display using a logarithmic scale (orders of magnitude).\n",
  "MAP transpose hover ms": "Transpose the plot layout (swap rows and columns).\nNon-transposed layouts are wide and suitable for data comparison.\nTransposed layouts are near-square and suitable for scatter plots.\n",
